SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets: the step of a walk back to the spine's first end is taken from the
stretch it walks, from its start to that end, as a forward walk's is
(mitcad#1397).

ComputeData shortens the walk's largest step to a fifth of the stretch it
walks where that stretch is short, the stretch taken as First to Last. A
forward walk to the spine's last end (intl) has them at its start and at
that end. A walk back to the spine's first end (intf) has First at that
end and Last at the guide's extension before it, a hundredth of the
guide, which ComputeData took for its stretch: such a walk's step was a
fifth of that, fifty times shorter than the same walk's forward.

The case: a box's top edges rounded with 1 meet in a mitre at a corner,
and the vertical edge below it and the mitre, one tangent chain, are
rounded with 1 too (two reported designs' items replayed). Over the mitre
the ball stays put, its centre on both cylinders' axes, its section
vanishing at the top. Where the spine runs from the top down, the mitre's
piece is walked back from the vertical edge's analytic piece to the top;
its contacts leave the cylinders' edges tangentially, so at a step of
0.004 on a guide of 1.9 they stayed on those edges within the tolerance,
the first step was taken for one leaving the faces and halved, and the
walk failed. The spine from the bottom up rounded it. Now the stretch of
a walk back to the first end runs from its start to First, and the walk
gets the forward walk's step: the corner is the ball's eighth either way.

diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_6.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_6.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_6.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_6.cxx
@@ -2609,10 +2609,19 @@
   TopoDS_Face bif;
   // Max step is relevant, but too great, the vector is required to detect
   // the twists.
-  if ((std::abs(Last - First) <= MS * 5.)
-      && (std::abs(Last - First) >= 0.01 * std::abs(NewFirst - Target)))
+  // (The stretch walked: First to Last, but a walk back to the spine's first
+  // end (intf) has First at that end and Last at the guide's extension before
+  // it, so its stretch runs from its start to First. Taken as First to Last,
+  // the extension, a hundredth of the guide, gave it a fifth of that as its
+  // step, fifty times shorter than the forward walk's: a contact leaving its
+  // face's edge tangentially, past a mitre between two roundings of the
+  // ball's radius, stayed on the edge within the tolerance at every first
+  // step tried, and the walk failed.)
+  const double aSpan =
+    (!Forward && !Inside && intf) ? std::abs(NewFirst - First) : std::abs(Last - First);
+  if ((aSpan <= MS * 5.) && (aSpan >= 0.01 * std::abs(NewFirst - Target)))
   {
-    MS = std::abs(Last - First) * 0.2;
+    MS = aSpan * 0.2;
   }
 
   while (again < 3)
